<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  Task 1 Safe Passage, ADVANCED and DISRUPTIVE tier.

  Alongside task1_safe_passage.xml, not replacing it: Core tier still has no
  aircraft, and the runner picks the file by parameter so both stay loadable.

  WHAT IS DIFFERENT FROM CORE, and why.

  1. THE AIRCRAFT OWNS THE PASSAGE. handbook 3.3.2 says that above Core the
     passage is only detectable from the air. So ENTRY, EXIT and every beacon
     state come from the plan, and the boat's own OAK-D only refines POSITION
     (nav::fusePassage). That is why there is no `observe` phase here: there is
     nothing to wait to see.

  2. THE AIRCRAFT ENDS THE LOOP, NOT GEOMETRY. Core used
     `Inverter(NearExit radius=8)`, which is a guess, and a wrong one: the boat
     must clear EVERY gate before the exit, and the exit buoy can sit well
     inside 8 m of the last one. Here the transit ends only when the UAV answers
     a request with 255/255, which PassageComplete reads.

  3. A NEW PLAN RESTARTS THE LEG. PlanChanged sits inside the leg's own
     ReactiveSequence, re-ticked at 10 Hz, so a revision halts the in-flight
     NavigateTo. The ForceSuccess around the leg is what makes that a RESTART
     rather than the end of the transit: without it a failed leg would fail
     KeepRunningUntilFailure and the boat would head for the exit mid-passage.

  4. A FAILED LEG RETRIES THE SAME GATE, it does not move on. MarkGateCleared
     is the last step of the leg, and RequestNextGate advances the sequence
     only when it ran. Anything that fails first (an AwaitGatePair timeout, an
     unusable pair, a PlanChanged re-task) leaves the gate un-cleared, so
     the next request asks for the SAME pair again and the aircraft, which
     answers a repeated sequence number idempotently, gives the same one back.

     Without that, the ForceSuccess in point 3 silently SKIPPED a gate on every
     retry: SITL on 2026-09-13 logged "re-planning this leg" and asked for the
     next gate 100 ms later, having never driven the one it was on.

  THE GUARD BAND is re-ticked every tick and halts everything below it in one
  tick. PassagePlanFresh is in it twice over: it is the handbook's "the UAV must
  report before the USV may transit" gate, AND the dead-link stop.

  TIMEOUT AND CANCEL live in bt_runner_node, not here.
  OBSTACLE AVOIDANCE lives in the autopilot, not here.
-->
<root BTCPP_format="4" main_tree_to_execute="SafePassageDisruptive">
  <BehaviorTree ID="SafePassageDisruptive">
    <ReactiveSequence name="guard_band">

      <IsAutonomous/>
      <PassagePlanFresh max_age_s="15.0"/>
      <ResolveBuoyStates/>
      <PublishSafePassageReport min_period_s="1.0"/>

      <Sequence name="passage">

        <SetTask token="TASK_SAFE_PASSAGE"/>

        <!-- The entry buoy is known from the plan the moment it arrives, so
             this drives straight at it instead of loitering to spot it. -->
        <CircleBuoy anchor="entry" radius="6.0" points="5" direction="cw"/>

        <ForceSuccess>
          <KeepRunningUntilFailure name="transit">
            <ReactiveSequence>

              <!-- FAILURE here ends the transit. It is the only thing that
                   should, and only the aircraft can say it. -->
              <Inverter>
                <PassageComplete/>
              </Inverter>

              <!-- One gate. Anything that fails inside restarts the leg. -->
              <ForceSuccess>
                <ReactiveSequence name="leg">
                  <Inverter>
                    <PlanChanged/>
                  </Inverter>
                  <Sequence>
                    <RequestNextGate/>
                    <AwaitGatePair timeout_s="5.0"/>
                    <GateWaypoint point="approach" standoff="6.0" approach="8.0" out="{goal}"/>
                    <NavigateTo target="port" goal="{goal}" tolerance="3.0"/>
                    <GateWaypoint point="through" standoff="6.0" approach="8.0" out="{goal}"/>
                    <NavigateTo target="port" goal="{goal}" tolerance="2.5"/>
                    <MarkGateCleared/>
                  </Sequence>
                </ReactiveSequence>
              </ForceSuccess>

            </ReactiveSequence>
          </KeepRunningUntilFailure>
        </ForceSuccess>

        <!-- From the plan, not from perception. Fails only if the aircraft
             never sent an exit at all. -->
        <ExitResolved/>
        <CircleBuoy anchor="exit" radius="6.0" points="5" direction="ccw"/>

      </Sequence>
    </ReactiveSequence>
  </BehaviorTree>
</root>
